23. Explain Hashing(Correctly)?
Hashing is a technique used to store and retreive data quickly using a key-value pair.
Java uses hashing in HashMap.

HashMap<String, String> data = new HashMap<>();
data.put("username", "admin");

Internally, HashMap uses a hash function to convert keys into hash codes, which decides where the data is stored in memory.
In my framework, I used Hashmap to store:
1. TestData
2. Environment details
3. API Response values
This avoids looping and improves performance.

24. Explain WebDriver Architecture? (Internal Working)
WebDriver follows a client-server architecture.
Flow:
1. Test Script(Java Code)
2. Selenium WebDriver API
3. Browser Driver(ChromeDriver)
4. Actual Browser
WebDriver acts as a bridge between Selenium and the browser.
This explains why driver version compatibility is important.

