32. What is Page Object Model(POM)?
Page Object Model is a design pattern where every web page is represented as a seperate class.
Each Class contain:
1. WebElement locator
2. Reusable methods
Example:
public class LoginPage {
  @FindBy(id="username")
  private WebElement element;

  public void login() {
  }
}

Advantages:
1. Fast Execution
2. Better Debugging
3. Less maintenance
4. Reusability methods
In my proect, POM help us manage large-scale application efficient.
